* @title Real overflow raises a recoverable arithmetic error
* @nonstandard Snoflake REAL is single precision; CSNOBOL4 uses double precision
* @expect >>>
* overflow failed cleanly
* still running
* <<<
* A real lives in one 32-bit cell, so it overflows near 3.4e38 where CSNOBOL4's
* double would yield inf. The overflow is a recoverable arithmetic error: with
* &ERRLIMIT set the multiply fails to its F goto and the run continues, and the
* interpreter never throws.
	&ERRLIMIT = 1000
	BIG = 1000000.0
	BIG = BIG * BIG
	BIG = BIG * BIG
	OUTPUT = BIG * BIG			:S(S)F(F)
S	OUTPUT = 'overflow did not happen'	:(A)
F	OUTPUT = 'overflow failed cleanly'
A	OUTPUT = 'still running'
END
